flowchart TB
    accTitle: Playback observes; execution replay acts again
    accDescr: The original immutable event log has two different uses. Read-only playback formats saved events and performs no tool calls. Execution replay extracts recorded model responses, feeds them to FakeModel, and executes only approved disposable local tools in a new clean fixture. That execution creates a new run ID and new event log. Compare normalized decisions and output hashes with the original, leaving its log and workspace unchanged.
    L["Original immutable log"] --> P["Read-only playback"]
    P --> V["Display saved events; no tools"]
    L --> F["Recorded responses to FakeModel"]
    W["New clean fixture"] --> R["Execute approved local tools"]
    F --> R
    R --> N["New run ID and log"]
    N --> C["Compare normalized decisions and outputs"]
    L --> C
